--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
R-squared (HC3):              0.0205
R-squared (Clustered):        0.0205

Notes: Model A uses HC3 heteroskedasticity-consistent standard errors (default).
Model B uses firm-level clustering to account for multiple breaches per firm.
Coefficients are identical across models; only standard errors differ.

Key Finding: Clustering makes standard errors LARGER (more conservative) but does not
change the significance of main findings. All significant effects remain significant
(or become more significant) when using firm-clustered SEs.

Significance levels: * p<0.10, ** p<0.05, *** p<0.01, ns = not significant


